# Imperatives — Memory Drill

## Purpose

Drill perfective imperative forms of high-frequency verbs. Most are irregular — the form cannot be predicted from the present or aorist stem. Must be memorised as frozen forms.

Prompt format: English command → Greek imperative (sg)
Example: "Come!" → "Έλα!"

## Why this belongs in memory drills

Regular imperative formation (-ε or -σε ending) is learnable as a rule. These forms are not regular. Each must be memorised individually. They appear constantly in real speech and cannot be avoided.

## Phase 3 core set

Implemented as 15 items in `imperatives.tsx`. Every `greek` string keeps its `!`, which
`matchPhonetic` strips before comparing.

| English prompt (`label`) | Imperative sg | Present     | Category | Notes |
|--------------------------|---------------|-------------|----------|-------|
| Come!                    | Έλα!          | έρχομαι     | tier-a   | Suppletive — completely different stem |
| Say! / Tell me!          | Πες!          | λέω         | tier-a   | Irregular |
| Give!                    | Δώσε!         | δίνω        | tier-a   | Semi-irregular |
| Bring!                   | Φέρε!         | φέρνω       | tier-a   | Irregular |
| Do it! / Make it!        | Κάνε!         | κάνω        | tier-a   | Regular pattern but high-frequency anchor |
| Take! / Pick up!         | Πάρε!         | παίρνω      | tier-b   | Irregular |
| Eat!                     | Φάε!          | τρώω        | tier-b   | Suppletive |
| Drink!                   | Πιες!         | πίνω        | tier-b   | Suppletive |
| Look! / Watch!           | Κοίτα!        | κοιτάζω     | tier-b   | Truncated form used in speech; Κοίταξε! is not accepted |
| Wait!                    | Περίμενε!     | περιμένω    | tier-b   | Regular |
| Write!                   | Γράψε!        | γράφω       | tier-b   | Regular -ψε |
| Read!                    | Διάβασε!      | διαβάζω     | tier-b   | Regular -σε |
| Listen!                  | Άκουσε!       | ακούω       | tier-b   | Regular -σε |
| Go!                      | Πήγαινε!      | πηγαίνω     | tier-b   | Imperfective form used; πήγαινε not πήγε |
| Find!                    | Βρες!         | βρίσκω      | tier-b   | Irregular |

## Plural imperatives (secondary)

Greek adds -τε for plural/formal imperatives. Drill singular first; introduce plural forms once singular is automatic. The pattern is mostly predictable once you know the singular.

## Drill modes

**Forward**: English command → Greek imperative (singular)
  - "Come! →?" → "Έλα!"

**Reverse**: Greek imperative → English, self-assess
  - "Πες! →?" → "Say! / Tell me!"

## Grouping

Filter categories: "Tier A (5)" (`tier-a`: Έλα, Πες, Δώσε, Φέρε, Κάνε) and "Tier B (10)"
(`tier-b`: the rest). The config screen's "All" button drills all 15.

## Time limits

No per-drill limit. Timing is the learner's Fast 4 s / Medium 6 s / Relaxed 8 s choice on the config
screen, plus 35% for each extra word in a forward answer (`src/routes/practice/components/drill-speeds.ts`).
Every answer here is one word, so the surcharge never applies.

## Notes

- Present these as vocabulary items, not grammar transformations — do not show the paradigm table, just the command form
- Negative imperative (Μην + subjunctive) is separate and should not be mixed into this drill
- Plural/formal forms (-τε) are predictable once singular known — note this but don't drill separately until Phase 3 is solid
